        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_CameraDefault">
            <English>Camera when opening</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_CameraDefault_Desc">
            <English>What the middle of the inventory shows\nwhen it opens: your soldier from the\nfront, as the arsenal does, or nothing -\nthe world as seen from his eyes. The\ncamera button in the header still turns\nit on or off while it is open.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_CameraDefault_Off">
            <English>Off (first person)</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_CameraDefault_Soldier">
            <English>Soldier (third person)</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_CellScale">
            <English>Tile scale</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_CellScale_Desc">
            <English>How large the cells and the pictures on\nthem are - above 1 if items are hard to\nmake out. The default, 1.1, lets a name\non a one-cell tile show more of its\nletters. Takes effect the next time the\ninventory opens. Where the columns would\nno longer fit across the screen, the\nlargest scale that fits is used.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_CompareTooltip">
            <English>Compare gear at the mouse</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_CompareTooltip_Desc">
            <English>A vest, uniform, helmet or backpack at\nthe mouse shows how it differs from\nthe one you wear: armor, room and\nweight. Green is better, red worse.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_DebugTiming">
            <English>Log window timings (debug)</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_DebugTiming_Desc">
            <English>Writes to the RPT how long each build\nand redraw took and how many controls\nthe display holds, what the window's\nframes cost in script (idle, mouse over\ntiles, dragging) and in which part, the\nwhole frame time (FPS), what each item\nfound by searching cost, and for each\ndrag its lift and frames - for reports\nof stutters and low FPS. Read as the\nwindow opens. Off in play.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandDrop">
            <English>Time to drop an item</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandDrop_Desc">
            <English>Seconds the hands are busy dropping one\nitem onto the ground (the drop key, a drag\nout of the window, Drop in the menu).\nEvery item waits its turn with a circle\non its tile: one runs at a time, the\nnext starts when it is done, and a click\non a circle cancels it. Closing the\nwindow cancels what still waits.\n\n0 drops at once, with no circle.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandEquip">
            <English>Time to put on or take off</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandEquip_Desc">
            <English>Seconds the hands are busy putting one\nitem on or taking it off: a drag onto a\nslot, a double click on the ground,\nEquip in the menu, Ctrl+click on a slot.\nThe circle lies on the tile or the slot;\na click on it cancels the action.\nClosing the window cancels what still\nwaits.\n\n0 does it at once, with no circle.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandMove">
            <English>Time to move to another container</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_HandMove_Desc">
            <English>Seconds the hands are busy moving one\nitem to a different container or holder:\na drag between containers, the quick\nmove, Take all and Put all in - one\ncircle per item, one after another. A\nclick on a circle cancels it.\nRearranging within a container, turning\nand splitting a stack take no time.\n\n0 moves at once, with no circle.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_LootSide">
            <English>Where other storage opens</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_LootSide_Desc">
            <English>Where the column of what you loot (a
crate, a vehicle, a body, the ground or
what lies nearby) opens.

Left of my storage: your own storage
column never moves, and the new column
opens beside it, in the middle of the
window.

Right of my storage: the new column takes
the right edge and your storage moves
aside for it, as in earlier versions.

An open window changes at its next
build.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_LootSide_Left">
            <English>Left of my storage - my storage stays put</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_LootSide_Right">
            <English>Right of my storage - my storage moves aside</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MagazineFillBar">
            <English>Fill bar on magazines</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MagazineFillBar_Desc">
            <English>A thin bar along the bottom of every\nmagazine that is not full: how many\nrounds are left, at a glance - on its\ntile and on a weapon's magazine slot.\n\nThe rounds as words have a switch of\ntheir own (Rounds on magazines).</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MagazineText">
            <English>Rounds on magazines</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MagazineText_Desc">
            <English>The rounds left in a magazine as words\n("17/30") in a corner of its tile. Off,\nthe fill bar alone tells how full one\nis - and a full one shows neither.\n\nA weapon's magazine slot keeps them.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MoveToStop">
            <English>Moving stops looting</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MoveToStop_Desc">
            <English>A movement key pressed while looting or\nsearching closes the window: the search\nstops and the soldier walks off. What\nwas found stays found; the item being\nsearched starts again next time.\n\nOff: movement keys do nothing in the\nwindow.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteContainers">
            <English>Mute button: containers</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteContainers_Desc">
            <English>The speaker in the window's header also\nsilences containers, kits and pouches\nbeing opened and closed.\n\nOff: these keep playing while the\nspeaker is muted.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteMagazines">
            <English>Mute button: magazines</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteMagazines_Desc">
            <English>The speaker in the window's header also\nsilences magazines being loaded,\nunloaded, reloaded and repacked.\n\nOff: these keep playing while the\nspeaker is muted.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteMoves">
            <English>Mute button: item moves</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteMoves_Desc">
            <English>The speaker in the window's header also\nsilences items being picked up, moved,\ndropped, put on, taken off, attached\nand turned.\n\nOff: these keep playing while the\nspeaker is muted.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteOther">
            <English>Mute button: other sounds</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteOther_Desc">
            <English>The speaker in the window's header also\nsilences the rest: inspecting an item\nand the click or warning when\nsomething is refused.\n\nOff: these keep playing while the\nspeaker is muted.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteSearch">
            <English>Mute button: searching</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_MuteSearch_Desc">
            <English>The speaker in the window's header also\nsilences the rustle while loot is\nsearched and the sound of an item\nfound.\n\nOff: these keep playing while the\nspeaker is muted.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PageRows">
            <English>Rows per page of a container</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PageRows_Desc">
            <English>How many rows of a tall crate or vehicle
are shown at a time. Taller than that, it
gets pages: a bar under it turns them,
and a fade on the page's edge with a
chip such as +37 items on other pages
says there is more. The search finds
items on any page, and an item held over
an arrow of the bar turns the page.

A page is at least 4 rows. 0 or 40 shows
the whole container, with its empty rows
folded as before. Only for what you
loot, not for your own gear.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonItems">
            <English>Take and put items</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonItems_Desc">
            <English>Who may take items out of a living\nperson's uniform, vest and backpack,\nand put items in. Vanilla lets anyone\ntake from a backpack.\n\nNobody: the gear can only be looked at.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonNotify">
            <English>Tell the searched player</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonNotify_Desc">
            <English>A player whose gear is opened reads\nwho is going through it. With a\nbackpack on, everyone near hears ACE's\nzipper and the player feels a tug.\n\nSwitched off, only ACE's own backpack\ninteraction still zips.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonOpen">
            <English>Open the whole person</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonOpen_Desc">
            <English>Whose uniform, vest and backpack open\nwith &quot;Inventory&quot; while they are alive.\nAnyone else opens only by the backpack,\nas in vanilla - but from any side.\n\nCaptives are surrendered or handcuffed\n(ACE). The unconscious always open\nwhole, as with ACE's &quot;Inventory&quot;.\n\nMission makers can close one person\nto everyone:\n_unit setVariable [&quot;einv_noAccess&quot;, true, true];</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonWorn">
            <English>Take off worn gear</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_PersonWorn_Desc">
            <English>Who may take off what a living person\nwears - weapons, helmet, uniform, vest,\nbackpack and the rest - by dragging,\nCtrl+click or the context menu.\n\nCaptives are surrendered or handcuffed\n(ACE). Bodies can always be stripped.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchBodies">
            <English>Search bodies</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchBodies_Desc">
            <English>What a body carries shows as &quot;?&quot;\nuntil it has been searched.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchContainers">
            <English>Search crates and vehicles</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchContainers_Desc">
            <English>What a crate or a vehicle holds shows\nas &quot;?&quot; until it has been searched.\n\nMission makers can leave out a single\nobject (an arsenal box, base supply):\n_box setVariable [&quot;einv_noSearch&quot;, true, true];</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchGround">
            <English>Search the ground</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchGround_Desc">
            <English>Loose items on the ground show as &quot;?&quot;\nuntil they have been searched.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchPersons">
            <English>Search living persons</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchPersons_Desc">
            <English>What a living person carries shows as\n&quot;?&quot; until it has been searched - awake,\nunconscious or captive alike.\n\nBodies follow &quot;Search bodies&quot;.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTime">
            <English>Search time per cell</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SearchTime_Desc">
            <English>Seconds it takes to search one grid\ncell of loot. A 2x2 item takes four\ntimes as long.\n\n0 shows everything at once.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_ShowNearby">
            <English>Show everything nearby</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_ShowNearby_Desc">
            <English>Shows every pile on the ground and\nevery crate within reach as a box of\nits own in the loot column, nearest\nfirst. Crates you did not open start\nfolded - click their name to open\nthem.\n\nOff: only what you opened shows, as\nin the vanilla inventory.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SoundVolume">
            <English>Volume</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SoundVolume_Desc">
            <English>How loud the inventory's sounds are for\nyou. The game's effects volume applies\non top, and so do earplugs and a blast's\ndeafness.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_Sounds">
            <English>Sounds</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SoundsWorld">
            <English>Others hear looting</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_SoundsWorld_Desc">
            <English>Players nearby hear someone loot: the\nrustle of a search, a rifle taken off a\nbody, a backpack dropped, a reload. Up\nto 10 to 20 metres, quieter than the\nlooter hears it.\n\nOff: only the looter hears anything.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_Sounds_Desc">
            <English>Every kind of gear sounds like what it\nis: weapons, magazines, vests, medical\nitems, helmets, radios and more - picked\nup, put down, put on, attached, loaded,\nand containers opened and searched.\n\nOff: you hear none of them. Others near\nyou may still hear you loot.</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_TileNames">
            <English>Item names on tiles</English>
        </Key>
        <Key ID="STR_einv_gui_Setting_TileNames_Desc">
            <English>The item's short name in the top\nright corner of every tile. Off, the\ntiles show the picture alone - the\nname still shows at the mouse.\n\nThe Arsenal's panel follows it.</English>
        </Key>
